# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vla-entity-property-bridge — COM properties on entity-backed VLA-objects (DXF-group bridge)
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: cad-runtime
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: feature-vla-entity-property-bridge

* Progress

- *1.8.11 (2026-08-07): the bridge LANDED* for the SCHMS subset —
  =Handle= / =ObjectName= (read-only), =Layer=, =Linetype=, =Color=,
  =Lineweight=, =Thickness=, =TextString=, =TagString=,
  =PromptString=, =StyleName=, =Height=, =Rotation= (radians, the
  entget convention — no conversion), =Mode=, =Elevation=,
  =Name= / =EffectiveName= (INSERT), =X/Y/ZScaleFactor=,
  =InsertionPoint= / =TextAlignmentPoint= (VARIANT-wrapped double
  SAFEARRAYs), and =Alignment= (acAlignment enum over 72 + 73/74).
  The representation boundary was solved with runtime hooks
  (=*com-point-wrap-hook*= / =*com-point-unwrap-hook*=, installed by
  autolisp-builtins-core like =*vlax-collection-items-hook*=) instead
  of moving =safearray-data= down — no struct migration needed.
  Same release: entmake =BLOCK=/=ENDBLK= block-definition creation
  (see =entmake-symbol-table-records.issue=), main-space filtering of
  =ssget "X"= / =entlast= / top-level =entnext=, and the
  =(entnext (tblobjname "BLOCK" name))= block walk.
- *1.8.12 (2026-08-07): the method surface followed* — third SCHMS
  round failed on "AutoCAD.Block has no method named INSERTBLOCK".
  Landed: =InsertBlock= on space / block collections (instantiates an
  ATTRIB per non-constant ATTDEF, transformed to the placement, SEQEND
  closed; returns the reference), =GetAttributes= (VARIANT array of
  the ATTRIB objects, via the new =*com-objects-wrap-hook*=),
  =HasAttributes= (group 66), entity =Move= / =Rotate= / =Copy= /
  =Delete= / =Erase= / =Update=, =GetBoundingBox= with the vendor
  by-reference output symbols (assigned at the builtins layer), and
  the =vlax-invoke= / =vlax-get= / =vlax-put= builtins (plain-data
  contract). Subentity runs excluded from collection membership.
- *1.8.13 (2026-08-07): the classic block-contents walk* — fourth
  SCHMS round moved past all COM errors (1 OK / 5 FAIL: "attendu 2
  LINE dans le bloc sigfic, trouve 0"): the fixture checker walks the
  definition from the BLOCK table record. Landed: the vendors'
  =(-2 . <first-entity ename>)= group on BLOCK =tblsearch= /
  =tblnext= views, and =entget= on a symbol-table record's ename
  (record view + =(-1 . ename)= head + =-2= for blocks).
- *Remaining open:* confirm against the SCHMS =test-cad-clautolisp=
  re-run and extend the property table to what it still consumes
  (candidates: =TrueColor=, =Closed=, =MTextAttribute=, MTEXT
  =Rotation= units — SPEC-UNCERTAIN); vendor probes for the
  SPEC-UNCERTAIN notes (EffectiveName on dynamic blocks,
  entmakex-on-BLOCK, ENDBLK-terminated entnext walk, glyph-metric
  bounding boxes).

* Context

Split out of =vla-accessor-family.issue= while resolving the SCHMS
"AutoCAD.Document has no property named BLOCKS" failure (1.8.10,
2026-08-07). The document collections (Blocks / Layers / ModelSpace /
PaperSpace, generic Item / Count / Add / Delete) are now live and
drawing-backed, and =vlax-ename->vla-object= wraps any entity in an
identity-stable =AutoCAD.Entity= COM object.

That entity wrapper, however, carries an *empty* properties table:
every =vla-get-<prop>= / =vla-put-<prop>= on an entity-backed
VLA-object raises =:unknown-com-property=. The SCHMS+ corpus leans
heavily on exactly these accessors (counts from
=schms-call-inventory.md=): =vla-put-textstring= 188,
=vla-get-layer= 170, =vla-get-insertionpoint= 169, =vla-get-rotation=
154, =vla-put-height= / =vla-put-textalignmentpoint= 126 each,
=vla-put-alignment= 125, =vla-get-effectivename= 7, … This is the
most likely next headless blocker for =make test-cad-clautolisp= once
the Blocks fix ships.

* Problem

Entity COM properties must read and write the entity's DXF groups —
the mock stores entities as group-code lists — but three sub-problems
make this more than a table fill:

1. *Mapping + conversion.* Property ⇄ group with per-entity-kind rules
   and unit conversions, e.g. =Layer= ⇄ 8, =TextString= ⇄ 1 (TEXT /
   MTEXT / ATTRIB / ATTDEF), =TagString= ⇄ 2 (ATTRIB / ATTDEF),
   =Name= / =EffectiveName= ⇄ 2 (INSERT; EffectiveName = Name headless
   — no dynamic blocks in the mock), =Handle= ⇄ 5 (read-only),
   =ObjectName= ⇐ kind ("LINE" → "AcDbLine", INSERT →
   "AcDbBlockReference", …), =Color= ⇄ 62 (256 = ByLayer default),
   =Height= ⇄ 40, =Rotation= ⇄ 50 **with degrees (DXF) ⇄ radians
   (ActiveX) conversion**, =Alignment= ⇄ 72 + 73 (TEXT) / 74 (ATTRIB)
   via the acAlignment enum.
2. *Representation boundary.* Point-valued properties
   (=InsertionPoint=, =TextAlignmentPoint=, =GetBoundingBox=) are
   VARIANT-wrapped double SAFEARRAYs on the vendor side, and SCHMS
   consumes them through =vlax-variant-value= + =vlax-safearray->list=
   (196 / 203 uses). The =safearray-data= struct behind
   =autolisp-safearray= lives in *autolisp-builtins-core*
   (=api.lisp=), which =cador= cannot depend on (builtins-core is
   above the host layer). Either the safearray representation moves
   down into =autolisp-runtime= (where =autolisp-variant= /
   =autolisp-safearray= already live), or the bridge exposes points as
   a host-neutral pure value that the builtins layer wraps.
3. *Write-through.* =vla-put-<prop>= must mutate the entity data the
   same way =entmod= does (shared helpers, ename cache / al-view
   invariants preserved), and reject read-only properties (=Handle=,
   =ObjectName=, =EffectiveName=).

* Proposal

- Move =safearray-data= (struct + accessors + the
  doubles→safearray→variant builders) from
  =autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp= down to
  =clautolisp.autolisp-runtime= next to =autolisp-variant= /
  =autolisp-safearray=; keep re-exports so builtins code is untouched.
- In =cador/source/vlax-api.lisp=, extend =host-vlax-get-property= /
  =-put-property= / =-property-available-p= with an entity-backed
  branch: resolve =mock-com-object-backing-ename= → entity, then
  dispatch on a declarative property table
  =(NAME KINDS GROUP READ-ONLY-P ENCODER DECODER)= covering the SCHMS
  subset above first.
- Classify each mapping per AGENTS.md § Dialect Divergence before
  coding (Rotation radians and the acAlignment enum are documented
  vendor behaviour; anything less certain gets a SPEC-UNCERTAIN marker
  + an entry in =deferred-spec-research.issue=).
- Regression tests at the cador layer (property read/write round-trips
  against entget) and one end-to-end .lsp on =--host mock= exercising
  the ATTRIB rewrite pattern the SCHMS migrations use
  (=vla-get-tagstring= → =vla-put-textstring= →
  =vla-put-textalignmentpoint= → =vla-put-alignment=).

* Acceptance criteria

- =(vla-get-layer (vlax-ename->vla-object e))= and friends work on
  =--host mock= for the mapped subset; unknown properties still raise
  =:unknown-com-property=.
- Point-valued getters return VARIANT(SAFEARRAY of doubles) consumable
  by =vlax-variant-value= / =vlax-safearray->list=; putters accept the
  same, plain lists, and =vlax-3d-point= results.
- Rotation converts degrees⇄radians; writes are visible to =entget=.
- SCHMS =make test-cad-clautolisp= progresses past any
  entity-property =:unknown-com-property= error (verified by pjb's
  re-run; adjust the mapped subset to what the suite actually
  consumes).
- Suite green on SBCL + CCL; RELEASE_NOTES + user-manual §ActiveX
  updated.
